# Counter base (ticket 28.7): the island's cabinet base under the worktop, 146 x 96 m, from the floor (y = -55) up to y = -1.2, just under the ground at y = 0, so it never
# shares a plane with it (the worktop-edge's flange closes the gap seen from the floor). Origin at the worktop's surface centre like kitchen-room, so the level places it at
# (0, 0, 0). Set 3 m back under the 152 x 102 m worktop: carcass 143.6 x 93.6, door fronts 1.2 m proud to 146 x 96, a plinth 3 m further back at the floor. Sage doors and
# drawer fronts, brass handles, on all four sides (7 doors along x, 5 along z). No collider (out of reach under the worktop). Detail 0.06 (about 1.2 m cells, near the floor of the
# format's detail) gives about 7.2k triangles at LOD0 (budget 6k): at detail 0.1 it was 11.4k, at 0.3 18.5k, the handles and door edges cost the most.
format 1
collider none

